  "findings": [
    "R9: original c411 production code passed with Luna high. It recovered from two advertised-but-unregistered STRONG tier errors and one manage_goal schema error. This pass cannot be attributed to later code repairs.",
    "R10: the first candidate failed with Luna high when the Parser worker hit the unchanged 4096 output-token limit. The incomplete proposal was not executed, and the unchanged two-child cap rejected a replacement. Its FAIL and raw evidence remain intact.",
    "R11: the final candidate passed with GPT-6.1 Sol medium. Both children completed and were collected, edited only their assigned modules, and ran 9 ParserTests / 3 AggregateTests. The parent integrated the CLI and the independent 17 tests plus 4 CLI cases passed.",
    "The only production-code change between R10 and R11 was excluding irrelevant work_contract guidance from requests with no actual tools; its regression test and development note were also updated. Model/effort changed too, so these runs are not a pure model-only controlled comparison.",
    "R11 provides one successful final-candidate engineering result, with zero failed tool receipts or incomplete model completions. One pass does not establish statistical superiority, repeatability, or an automatic model-upgrade policy.",
    "Each live engineering run uses the same configured model on parent and children. Heterogeneous read-only search/review role routing has separate deterministic HTTP integration evidence; these three runs are not a live heterogeneous-role benchmark.",
    "The product results for passing R9 and R11 remain unverified/not_run with task_succeeded=false. Independent post-run acceptance does not rewrite the earlier product verification state."
  ],
